  PASS  ...and UNALIGNABLE is not UNREADABLE, which is doctrine 88's whole complaint
          a refusal rate is uninterpretable until its causes are separated.
  PASS  a WEIGHT disagreement becomes a knowledge set, and arithmetic on it fails LOUDLY
          moras Readings({1, 2}). `san.moras()` is `sum(s.moras for s in sylls)`; a TypeError there is the correct outcome and a silently wrong sum is not. Refusing the whole word instead would be doctrine 24's error — deleting a category to protect a sum().

